Z||000000||Fformula88||04-28-2001||09:14 AM||||My Fiero is still suffering from a few symptoms... mostly when its cold.  At idle when its cold, it will idle poorly at times, sometimes stalling itself out.  But not often.  Usually its just a rough idle.  When at speed the car runs fine.  Its also running very rich when its first started and for a few minutes after until it wamrs up.  WOnce its warm, it will sometimes (maybe 50% of the time) idle a little rough, and otherwise idles perfectly.  <P>I am thinking that the rich condition is its biggest problem with the poor idle/stalling.  Vacumn lines are good, and it has new EGR tube, EGR valve, MAF, TPS, IAC, coolant and air temp sensors, plugs, wires, coil.  Any ideas on where I should be looking?  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||5
Z||000001||SteveJ||04-28-2001||09:20 AM||||Rich? O2 sensor.<P>Any codes?<P>When running does it stink? That's rich and the O2 sensor corrects it. . . and yes they run quite well when rich to the point where you get used to it and when you correct it the car seems weak when its fixed.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||04-28-2001||12:49 PM||||Does your engine have two coolant sensors? One for the gage and one for the ECM?<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000003||c m west||04-28-2001||01:35 PM||||faulty cold start injector switch - causing the injector to stay open, thereby adding more fuel||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fformula88||04-28-2001||01:36 PM||||The car has two coolant sensors... one for the guage replaced about three years ago and one for the ECM replaced about three weeks ago.<P>O2 sensor is fairly new.  It runs rich when first started, when the engine is cold and idling (like in the garage).  The ECM doesn't use O2 sensor imputs immediately and its unlikely thatrs the problem.  <P>When its idling it smokes and smells like unburnt fuel.  There is spark to all cylinders.<P>It may be that the car will run ok rich, but thats just going to create problems down the road.  Its already destroyed a cat converter,  and will continue to clog them up if its putting so much soot thru the exhaust.  If I rev it up after starting it, it will spit black soot out of the tailpipe!<P>I was initially thinking injectors, but since it runs much better after its heated up I am not so sure thats going to be the problem.  I wouldn't think it would be an intermittant problem if the timing was off.  Maybe a bad cylinder or lost compression?  Its times are good (0-60 in 8.7 with auto tranny seems about right).  I am stumped... Thanks for the ideas!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fformula88||04-28-2001||01:39 PM||||cm west... I hadn't thought of that!  Good idea!  I'll have to look into it!  Thanks!||||reg||1
